    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0809" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-15T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 17—10:30 a.m.]<anchor
                            n="22" xml:id="d426-f1"/></dateline></opener>
                <p>104. Liang’s leave extended 20 days. Chances of Pao Kuei-ching<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d426-f2"/> for the Premiership apparently increasing although press
                    alleges Chang Tso-lin desires to maintain Liang during Chang’s negotiations with
                    Canton Government because of financial position of Liang. Pao is favored by Wu
                    Pei-fu.</p>
                <p>Wu Pei-fu urges trial of Minister of Finance Chang Hu on the ground of the
                    proposed ninety six million salt surplus loan.</p>
                <p>Chang Tso-lin has made preparations for prompt movement of troops.
                    Representatives of all Northern factions assembled at Mukden on the occasion of
                    his birthday. C. C. Wu left Mukden on the 8th after 10 days’ visit.</p>
                <p>Teachers in primary schools besieging Ministry of Education for back pay.</p>
                <p>President has published circular telegram pointing out expiration of his term
                    next year and urgent necessity for election new Parliament to elect
                    successor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
